 "page_text_sample": "This is a list of words you need to study for the Japanese Language Proficiency Test Level N5.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nClick on each word for more details.\n\n\n浴びる (abiru): to take a shower\n\n\n危ない (abunai): dangerous, risky\n\n\nあげる (ageru): to give\n\n\n赤/赤い (aka/akai): red\n\n\n明るい (akarui): bright, colorful\n\n\n開ける (akeru): to open\n\n\n秋 (aki): autumn\n\n\n開く (aku): to open\n\n\n甘い (amai): sweet\n\n\n雨 (ame): rain\n\n\nあなた (anata): you\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n兄 (ani): older brother\n\n\n姉 (ane): older sister\n\n\n青い (aoi): blue\n\n\n洗う (arau): to wash\n\n\n有る (aru): to be, to exist\n\n\n歩く (aruku): to walk\n\n\n朝 (asa): morning\n\n\n朝ご飯 (asagohan): breakfast\n\n\n明後日 (asatte): day after tomorrow\n\n\n足 (ashi): foot, leg\n\n\n明日 (ashita): tomorrow\n\n\n遊ぶ (asobu): to play\n\n\n\n\nJLPT N5 Kanji Lesson #1: 人 (nin)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDownload the video lesson and transcript\n\n\n\n\nあそこ (asoko): there"
